  "title": "Dataset containing resting EEG for a sample of 103 normal infants in the first year of life",
  "description": "This dataset comprises resting-state electroencephalography (EEG) recordings from 103 typically developing infants during the first year of life, with a total of 130 recordings distributed across four sessions. The dataset includes both male (n=62) and female (n=41) participants and serves as a normative reference for early brain electrical activity and neurodevelopmental trajectories during infancy.",
  "methods_description": "Resting EEG recordings were collected from 103 normal infants in the first year of life. The dataset includes 130 total EEG recordings distributed across 4 sessions, with variable numbers of recordings per subject (ranging from 1 to 4 recordings per infant).",
